#section-title[What is Televoto]

Televoto is a web platform designed for organizers running *events with live voting*: talent
shows, artistic or sports competitions, hackathons, festivals, corporate or school contests. It
replaces paper ballots, spreadsheets, and manual counting with a real-time digital system,
accessible from a smartphone via a simple link or QR code — no app to download, no account to
create for voters.

#section-title[How it works, in 3 phases]

#card-grid(
  cols: 3,
  card(icon: "⚙️", title: "1 · Set up the event")[
    The organizer creates the event, adds the candidates/competitors, and generates the access
    codes for judges and the public.
  ],
  card(icon: "📲", title: "2 · Live voting")[
    Judges and the public receive a link or a QR code, open the page on their phone, and assign
    a score to each candidate.
  ],
  card(icon: "🏆", title: "3 · Ranking and reveal")[
    The final score is calculated automatically and revealed with a dedicated scenic effect:
    the Final Ranking.
  ],
)

#section-title[Key features]

#card-grid(
  cols: 2,
  card(icon: "⚖️", title: "Dual voting channel")[
    Qualified jury (weighted vote) and general public, combined with customizable weights per
    event (e.g. 70% jury / 30% public).
  ],
  card(icon: "🔐", title: "Single-use voting codes")[
    Every voter receives a unique code shared via link or QR, valid for one vote per candidate:
    no duplicate votes.
  ],
  card(icon: "📡", title: "Live dashboard")[
    The organizer sees in real time how many codes have been used and how voting is
    progressing, without needing to reload the page.
  ],
  card(icon: "🗂", title: "Multi-event management")[
    A central panel to organize multiple events, each with its own candidates, codes, and
    password, fully isolated from one another. Wrapped-up events archive in one click and can be
    cloned to restart from an already-ready format.
  ],
  card(icon: "📈", title: "Configurable scoring")[
    Weighted average between jury and public, with an optional "trimmed mean" to reduce the
    impact of anomalous or outlier votes.
  ],
  card(icon: "🎉", title: "Final Ranking")[
    A final-ranking reveal screen designed for the event's key moment, in front of the audience.
  ],
)

#pagebreak()

